From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: net2280: restart the NET2282 DMA after a short
 OUT packet

The NET2282 does not chain DMA descriptors: fill_dma_desc() and
start_queue() set END_OF_CHAIN on every descriptor unless PLX_2280,
and each OUT request is started by the "transaction done" interrupt of
the previous one (handle_stat1_irqs() -> restart_dma()).

A short OUT packet raises SHORT_PACKET_TRANSFERRED as soon as it enters
the FIFO, behind the last packets of the request being moved by DMA.
When that interrupt is handled before the "transaction done" of that
request shows in irqstat1 (read first, once per interrupt), the loop of
handle_ep_small() retires the request through scan_dma_completions(),
then waits for the FIFO to empty: nothing moves it, since the engine
stopped at the end of its chain. The loop leaves through the "stuck"
escape, writes DMA_ABORT to an idle engine and waits 50 us for
DMA_ENABLE to drop, which it does not; restart_dma() then hits the
WARN_ON() of start_dma(). On a FortiGate 100D (NET2282, CDC NCM gadget)
a sustained host-to-device transfer ends there, with the OUT endpoint
NAKing for good and the host timing out its transmit queue.

On the NET2282 only, once a request has retired in that loop, stop the
idle engine and start the new head of the queue as the dma interrupt
would have: start_dma() moves the short transfer found in the FIFO in
single mode and clears the stale dma status. With an empty queue, the
FIFO waits (NAKing) for the next request. Also report the DMA registers
when DMA_ENABLE does not drop after an abort, instead of the bare
WARN_ON() of start_dma().

NET2280 (chaining) and USB338x paths are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/net2280.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/net2280.c
@@ -851,6 +851,22 @@
 	handshake(&dma->dmactl, BIT(DMA_ENABLE), 0, 50);
 }
 
+/* like spin_stop_dma(), but say which state the engine was left in when
+ * DMA_ENABLE did not drop: start_dma() would warn without any detail
+ */
+static void spin_stop_dma_report(struct net2280_ep *ep, const char *why)
+{
+	struct net2280_dma_regs	__iomem *dma = ep->dma;
+
+	if (!handshake(&dma->dmactl, BIT(DMA_ENABLE), 0, 50))
+		return;
+	dev_warn_ratelimited(&ep->dev->pdev->dev,
+		"%s %s: dma still enabled, dmactl %08x dmastat %08x dmacount %08x dmadesc %08x ep_stat %08x ep_avail %u\n",
+		ep->ep.name, why, readl(&dma->dmactl), readl(&dma->dmastat),
+		readl(&dma->dmacount), readl(&dma->dmadesc),
+		readl(&ep->regs->ep_stat), readl(&ep->regs->ep_avail));
+}
+
 static inline void stop_dma(struct net2280_dma_regs __iomem *dma)
 {
 	writel(readl(&dma->dmactl) & ~BIT(DMA_ENABLE), &dma->dmactl);
@@ -2615,6 +2631,7 @@
 			struct net2280_request *stuck_req = NULL;
 			int	stopped = ep->stopped;
 			int	num_completed;
+			int	retired = 0;
 			int	stuck = 0;
 			u32	count;
 
@@ -2629,6 +2646,38 @@
 				 * dma handles (M >= N), may empty the queue
 				 */
 				num_completed = scan_dma_completions(ep);
+				retired += num_completed;
+
+				/* NET2282: without chaining (END_OF_CHAIN on
+				 * every descriptor, see fill_dma_desc()), the
+				 * engine stopped when the request(s) above
+				 * retired: no DMA moves the data now in the
+				 * fifo, which belongs to the next request
+				 * (the short packet raised this irq before
+				 * the "transaction done" of the previous one
+				 * was seen in irqstat1). Waiting for the fifo
+				 * would only end through the "stuck" escape,
+				 * then DMA_ABORT on an idle engine whose
+				 * DMA_ENABLE does not drop. Stop the idle
+				 * engine and start the new head as the dma irq
+				 * would have: start_dma() moves the short
+				 * transfer in single mode and clears the stale
+				 * dma status. With an empty queue, the fifo
+				 * waits (NAKing) for the next net2280_queue().
+				 */
+				if (retired && !ep->out_overflow &&
+				    (ep->dev->quirks & (PLX_LEGACY | PLX_2280))
+						== PLX_LEGACY) {
+					writel(readl(&ep->dma->dmactl) &
+						~BIT(DMA_ENABLE),
+						&ep->dma->dmactl);
+					spin_stop_dma_report(ep, "short out");
+					ep->stopped = stopped;
+					if (!list_empty(&ep->queue))
+						restart_dma(ep);
+					return;
+				}
+
 				if (unlikely(list_empty(&ep->queue) ||
 						ep->out_overflow)) {
 					req = NULL;
@@ -2678,7 +2727,7 @@
 
 			/* stop DMA, leave ep NAKing */
 			writel(BIT(DMA_ABORT), &ep->dma->dmastat);
-			spin_stop_dma(ep->dma);
+			spin_stop_dma_report(ep, "abort");
 
 			if (likely(req)) {
 				req->td->dmacount = 0;
